#   "its own package.json file" and "its own build tool configuration", so "an independent build process and an
#   independent deploy / CI". Microservices and microfrontends have in common "Independent builds and deployments":
#   https://single-spa.js.org/docs/microfrontends-concept
# - single-spa, performance: "Microfrontends are often more performant than the monoliths from which they originate.
#   This is due to built-in lazy loading". "One important performance consideration is to share a single instance of
#   large libraries (such as React, Vue, or Angular), which is highly encouraged":
#   https://single-spa.js.org/docs/microfrontends-concept
# - single-spa, shared libraries: "for large libraries like react, momentjs, rxjs, etc, you may consider making them
#   shared dependencies":
#   https://single-spa.js.org/docs/recommended-setup
# - Module Federation docs, use cases: "Large Applications", "Microfrontend Architecture" and "Multi-team Development"
#   ("Module Federation can assist multiple teams in collaboratively developing large applications"):
#   https://module-federation.io/guide/start/index.html
# - React, two copies of React break hooks ("This may happen if you accidentally end up with two copies of the react
#   package"; "You might have more than one copy of React in the same app"):
#   https://react.dev/warnings/invalid-hook-call-warning
